What is Logistic Regression and why is it appropriate for my problem?
- Logistic Regression is a machine learning method that's used to predict between two possible outcomes. It looks at the information in the
  dataset and uses patterns in that information to predict which of the two outcomes is more likely.
- Logistic Regression works well for my dataset because I am trying to predict whether a loan application will be approved or rejected. 
  Since there are only two possible outcomes, this is a binary classification problem. The model can use information such as income, loan
  amount, credit score, employment status, and asset values to help predict whether a loan will be approved or rejected.
